# Never fake FPGA-SIM

Words: [README.md — Words used](../../README.md#words-used-in-this-project).
This is **copy 1** of the RAM / “FPGA-SIM is the chip” law (copy 2:
[docs/FPGA_FIT.md](../../docs/FPGA_FIT.md) NEVER table).

**FPGA-SIM** = Field-Programmable Gate Array simulation: **Verilator** of
the **same** `rtl/*.sv` (Register-Transfer Level) as
`make -C tools/board_flow bit`. F9 FPGA-SIM **is** the chip. Default:
`runtime/sim_backend.py`. GUI shows `FPGA-SIM (RTL)` vs `(HOST)`. Host
twin (`JMR_SIM_HOST=1`) is opt-in debug only — never a quiet fallback
when the RTL binary is missing (fail loud: `make -C sim sim_server_synth`).
Do not pretend PYTHON is FPGA-SIM.

Legal SRAM first, then glass. Do not make a title playable on a
Verilator-only heap and “flatten later.” The user runs `make bit` — **never
the agent** (`source scripts/vivado_env.sh && make -C tools/board_flow bit`
on the host). Do not start Vivado to check. Inspect the parent and
**exec64** — the only decoder since 2026-08-21. `sim_server_synth` PASS is
not a bitstream.

Glass is **640×480** (GUI mirror matches HDMI, not a 16-line strip).
Keyboard is **full JS** (case + punctuation); do not reintroduce an a–z fold.

**Vivado RAM is UG901, not agent homework.** Citations: *Vivado Design Suite
User Guide: Synthesis (UG901) 2026.1* — [Simple Dual-Port Block RAM with
Single Clock (Verilog)](https://docs.amd.com/r/en-US/ug901-vivado-synthesis/Simple-Dual-Port-Block-RAM-with-Single-Clock-Verilog)
(`simple_dual_one_clock.v`), [Single-Port Block RAM Write-First
(Verilog)](https://docs.amd.com/r/en-US/ug901-vivado-synthesis/Single-Port-Block-RAM-Write-First-Mode-Verilog)
(`rams_sp_wf.v`), [RAM_STYLE](https://docs.amd.com/r/en-US/ug901-vivado-synthesis/RAM_STYLE),
[Case Statement](https://docs.amd.com/r/en-US/ug901-vivado-synthesis/Case-Statement)
(`unique` → `parallel_case`), [Blocking and Non-Blocking
Assignments](https://docs.amd.com/r/en-US/ug901-vivado-synthesis/Blocking-and-Non-Blocking-Assignments),
[AR 56457](https://adaptivesupport.amd.com/s/article/56457) (RAM in its own
hierarchy matching the template), [AR 58025](https://adaptivesupport.amd.com/s/article/58025)
(Synth **8-3967** async-read template miss). Fit: [FPGA_FIT.md](../../docs/FPGA_FIT.md).
Live leftovers: [SESSION_HANDOFF.md](../../docs/SESSION_HANDOFF.md).

Live caps (PYTHON + RTL, 2026-08-21 fit): `MAX_OBJ=960`, arrays
`1536×32 + 12×128`, `ENV_DEPTH=384`, `CODE_WORDS=20480`, `MAX_SPR=16`.
Do not restore `8192`/`4096`. JS heap is not the 4 MB **ASET** (asset)
bank. `cls_*` 16×16 stays. `storage_engine` `linebuf` 8-4767 is a small
**FAT** copy buffer — leave it. Copy working **Port A** (legal Block RAM
shape): `jmr_video_vram.sv` / `jmr_mini_fb.sv`. Numbers:
[FPGA_FIT.md](../../docs/FPGA_FIT.md).

## Rules that are actually AMD (do not ship a diff that breaks one)

1. **Big memories: tiny write process, not the VM FSM.** Copy
   `jmr_mini_fb.sv` / `jmr_video_vram.sv` Port A. Any large unpacked array
   (today: `spr_mem`, `name_mem` 32K,
   `json_mem` 8K, `stack` 2048×32, `name_hash_tbl` 1024×16, `varr_len`,
   `vobj_alloc`, `vvars` — and any new buffer in that class; `imgd_pix`
   moved to external SRAM 2026-08-21) is:
   `always_ff if (we) mem[waddr] <= wdata; rdata <= mem[raddr];` with
   **scalar** we/addr/data. The parent FSM / case only sets those strobes.
   Do not put `mem[i] <=` back in the 7k-line `always_ff` (glass, HEAP,
   exec, new opcode — same rule). Isolated `*_rdata` reads **without**
   moving those writes still blew **71 GB** (15:22). Writes moved out
   (15:32) → ~**15 GB** hold after `e32_p_clr` instead of 8→36→70.
   Heap tables `stack` / `name_hash_tbl` / `varr_len` / `vobj_alloc` /
   `vvars` use the same Port A. **Glass / title debug uses those tasks.
   Do not put `stack[i] <=` / `vobj_alloc[i] <=` back to make a game
   paint.** FOREACH el+idx is two clocks (`stack_dual_pend`). `arr_len` /
   `vobj_cls` still FSM-poked (Synth 8-13159 dissolved them to FFs) — if
   you touch those, same Port A, do not add more `mem[i] <=`. **LUTRAM
   leftovers (16:17 map log, not the 70 GB hang):** `source_mem` (reset +
   gated read in the RAM process), `vconsts` / `vobj_proto` (FSM
   `mem[i] <=` + mux read). Same Port A. Do not “fix” with `ram_style`
   while the poke stays. Recipe: [FPGA_FIT.md](../../docs/FPGA_FIT.md)
   LUTRAM leftovers. `ram_style = "block"` does not save an FSM poke. Mux
   **addresses**, not forty `rdata <= mem[f()]` in one process. Template
   miss → 8-3967 / 8-4767 (RAM as FFs = 70 GB) or LUTRAM (mapping cost).

2. **Do not mix blocking `=` and NBA `<=` in one sequential block** (UG901
   Blocking and Non-Blocking Assignments).

3. **`unique case` is `parallel_case`** (UG901 Case Statement). Every arm
   is built in parallel. A `unique case` that combo-reads a large unpacked
   array is N RAM ports / a giant mux. Use plain `case` on opcode/`nid`.
   Sequential `case (state)` is fine if it does not combo-index BRAM.

4. **Do not reset-clear a BRAM in one cycle.** AR 58025 / UG949: extra reset
   on the RAM or its read-address register breaks inference. Walk one index
   per clock (`HEAP_CLR`). A `for` over `MAX_OBJ` in `always_comb` or in
   reset unrolls to parallel compares/writes.

5. **This machine (not UG901):** one JS heap in the parent (`one-heap-keep-gen`);
   exec address in, `*_rdata` next clock; no unpacked array ports; no
   `` `ifdef SYNTHESIS `` smaller heap; no `RAMB36` inside the VM.
   **Extract only control into submodules** (user decision 2026-08-22): a
   submodule owns NO arrays and reaches the single heap solely through
   scalar address/data/we ports with registered reads (`*_rdata` next
   clock) — the `u_exec64` shape. Duplicating any heap array inside a
   submodule stays forbidden. Why the old blanket ban was relaxed: it was
   never an AMD constraint — it existed to stop a second heap copy, which
   the replacement still stops — and it blocked the largest remaining fit
   lever. Measured 2026-08-22: u_exec64 (submodule) runs 4.19 logic
   LUTs/FF; the flat 112-state parent runs 11.00; bringing the parent's
   56,604 registers toward exec64's ratio is worth ~385k LUTs of the
   ~660k still needed. u_exec64 is the existence proof: 0 BRAM, 174
   LUTRAM, holds no heap.
   `sim_server_synth` PASS is Verilator. `e32_p_clr` 8-6014 is unused-FF
   housekeeping, not the hang. Kill synth only when the log is frozen **and**
   RSS is still climbing toward ~80 GB.

```systemverilog
// GOOD — same shape as jmr_mini_fb Port A (tasks already in jmr_js_vm.sv)
always_ff @(posedge clk) begin
  if (we) ram[waddr] <= wdata;
  rdata <= ram[raddr];  // raddr is a scalar wire
end
// FSM / unique case only (glass, HEAP, new opcode — same):
stack_wr(sp, alu_r, tag);
vobj_alloc_wr(valloc_i[9:0], 2'd1);
varr_len_wr(aid, len);
name_hash_wr(idx, h);
vvars_wr(slot, val);
json_putc(ch);
imgd_we <= 1'b1; imgd_waddr <= imgd_i; imgd_wdata <= pix;

// BAD — 70 GB / extra RAM port: poke from the 7k-line FSM
imgd_pix[imgd_i] <= fb_dump_back;
stack[sp] <= alu_r;
vobj_alloc[valloc_i] <= 2'd1;
// BAD — two stack writes one cycle (FOREACH uses stack_dual_pend, extra clock)
stack_wr(sp, el, t0);
stack_wr(sp + 8'd1, idx, t1);
```
